# Published artifacts. NEM.CLI writes these; nobody edits them by hand, and a rerun rewrites
# millions of lines across a few hundred files. Left to itself GitHub tries to diff all of it,
# gives up ("this diff is taking too long to generate"), and then renders nothing at all — the
# handful of source files in the same pull request included.
#
# -diff compares them by hash instead of by content, so the source diff survives a data refresh.
# linguist-generated keeps them out of the language stats and collapses them in review.
#
# `git diff --text` still produces a real diff locally when one is genuinely wanted; the artifacts
# are plain JSON and the tooling that reads them is unaffected by anything declared here.
NEM.Web/wwwroot/data/**/*.json -diff linguist-generated=true

# Shell scripts run on Linux build agents (Cloudflare Pages runs NEM.Web/build.sh and
# docs/build.sh). A CRLF checkout on Windows must not reach the index, or the shebang line
# carries a stray carriage return and the script fails to execute.
*.sh text eol=lf
